WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.843
Notifications tell users that something happened on the site.

00:00:04.843 --> 00:00:09.603
This video shows how they reach the notification center, how a workflow sends

00:00:09.603 --> 00:00:13.790
them, and how each user chooses to receive them by email or by SMS.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.850
Every notification is stored for the user it is meant for.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.905
Users read their notifications in the admin, from the bell in the top

00:00:25.905 --> 00:00:28.230
bar and from the notification center.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.350
A notification can also be sent by email or by SMS, through notification methods.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.930
Each user decides which of the methods they receive.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:43.701
Workflows send notifications without any code, and a module can send them for

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.395
the events it handles.

00:00:45.395 --> 00:00:48.420
Each user sees only their own notifications.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.256
Three features in the Notifications category provide notifications.

00:00:57.256 --> 00:01:01.170
Let's open Tools, Features, and search for notifications.

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.973
Notifications provides the notification center.

00:01:04.973 --> 00:01:10.455
Email Notifications and SMS Notifications are the two methods, and they depend on

00:01:10.455 --> 00:01:12.534
the Email and SMS features.

00:01:12.994 --> 00:01:16.024
Let's select the three features and enable them.

00:01:16.024 --> 00:01:19.334
Once they are enabled, a bell appears in the top bar.

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:28.415
With the Workflows feature enabled, a workflow can send notifications.

00:01:28.415 --> 00:01:34.894
Let's open Design, Workflows, and the workflow named Notify the editors when a page is published.

00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:39.474
It starts with the Content Published event, limited to pages.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:44.939
When a page is published, the workflow continues to the Notify Specific Users task.

00:01:45.394 --> 00:01:48.331
Double-click the task to open its settings.

00:01:48.331 --> 00:01:53.186
User names takes a comma-separated list of the users to notify, and Subject

00:01:53.186 --> 00:01:55.524
is the title of the notification.

00:01:55.975 --> 00:02:01.657
Summary is a short description, and Text Body and HTML Body hold the message.

00:02:01.657 --> 00:02:03.847
URL and Type are optional.

00:02:03.847 --> 00:02:07.475
Most fields accept Liquid, a template language.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.624
The toolbox lists the tasks you can add.

00:02:10.624 --> 00:02:13.204
Searching for notifications finds two:

00:02:13.204 --> 00:02:19.067
Notify Specific Users, and Notify Content Owner, which notifies the owner of the content item.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:24.320
To run the workflow, let's publish a draft page from Content, Content Items.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:29.110
The Content Published event starts the workflow, and the users are notified.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:38.136
The bell in the top bar counts the notifications you have not read, in a badge.

00:02:38.136 --> 00:02:41.640
Users need the Manage notifications permission to see it.

00:02:42.098 --> 00:02:45.327
Open the bell to see the unread notifications.

00:02:45.327 --> 00:02:49.488
Each one shows its subject, its summary, and when it arrived.

00:02:49.953 --> 00:02:54.703
At the bottom of the menu, Notification Center opens the full list.

00:02:59.003 --> 00:03:03.725
The notification center lists all your notifications, the most recent first.

00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:07.353
Unread ones are highlighted, and their subjects are bold.

00:03:07.814 --> 00:03:12.680
Each row shows the subject, the summary, and when the notification arrived.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:15.684
Mark as read marks one notification as read.

00:03:16.139 --> 00:03:20.044
The search box finds text in the summary and the text body.

00:03:20.044 --> 00:03:25.329
Show filters the list to Read or Unread notifications, and Sort changes the order.

00:03:25.785 --> 00:03:30.350
Actions, View opens a notification on its own page, with its text, and

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:31.732
marks it as read.

00:03:31.732 --> 00:03:34.735
Mark as unread and Delete are at the bottom.

00:03:35.197 --> 00:03:39.338
To work on several notifications, select their check boxes.

00:03:39.338 --> 00:03:44.627
Actions then offers Mark as read, Mark as unread, and Remove for all of them.

00:03:45.079 --> 00:03:49.752
Mark All as Read, next to the search box, marks every notification as

00:03:49.752 --> 00:03:51.559
read after you confirm.

00:03:55.859 --> 00:04:00.030
Each user chooses how they receive notifications on their own profile.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:02.719
Let's open the user menu, and then Profile.

00:04:03.174 --> 00:04:08.175
Notification Methods lists Email Notifications and SMS Notifications.

00:04:08.175 --> 00:04:12.844
A checked method sends a copy of every notification to the user.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.340
Let's clear SMS Notifications and select Save.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:22.420
The user keeps receiving notifications by email, and the notification center always receives them.

00:04:22.883 --> 00:04:27.883
Email Notifications sends to the Email field of the user, and SMS Notifications

00:04:27.883 --> 00:04:29.765
to the Phone Number field.

00:04:29.765 --> 00:04:33.765
When a field is empty, that method fails for the user, and the

00:04:33.765 --> 00:04:36.823
notification stays in the notification center.

00:04:41.023 --> 00:04:46.694
Email Notifications sends through the Email service, so a provider must be configured

00:04:46.694 --> 00:04:49.374
under Settings, Communication, Email.

00:04:49.374 --> 00:04:53.674
The email carries the Text Body, or the HTML Body when Use HTML

00:04:53.674 --> 00:04:57.413
Body when possible is checked and an HTML Body is set.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:05:03.789
SMS Notifications sends through the SMS service, so choose the Default SMS provider

00:05:03.789 --> 00:05:06.381
under Settings, Communication, SMS.

00:05:06.381 --> 00:05:09.542
The text message carries only the Text Body.

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:12.133
Separate videos cover each service.

00:05:12.883 --> 00:05:16.848
The notification always stays in the notification center.

00:05:16.848 --> 00:05:21.316
A notification task of a workflow ends with Done when an email or

00:05:21.316 --> 00:05:25.281
SMS was sent, with Failed when none was, and with Failed:

00:05:25.281 --> 00:05:28.553
no user found when it finds no user to notify.

00:05:30.553 --> 00:05:36.920
Notifications reach users in the notification center, and by email and SMS as each user chooses.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.543
Thanks for watching.

